# Emulator-only configuration.
#
# **Every value here is fake, and this file is committed on purpose.**
#
# Firebase reads `.env.local` only for the local emulator suite, never deploys
# it, and lets it take precedence over `.env`. That precedence is the point:
# `functions/.env` holds the real project's values, including a redirect URI
# pointing at the deployed site — so without this file the local OAuth flow
# sends the browser to production, where the callback answers 404. It looks
# like a broken app and is a configuration bug.
#
# It also **overrides only the keys it defines**. Anything omitted falls through
# to `.env`, which is how the real credentials stay out of git.
#
# `.gitignore` carries a deliberate exception for this path, and
# `src/hl/envLocal.spec.ts` asserts what is committed here still works from a
# fresh clone — nothing else can notice, because the test suites set their own
# overrides and pass either way.

FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=hl-genesis

# Emulator-only. A state sealed with the production key would be openable by the
# production callback, so this is deliberately not that key.
OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=emulator-only-state-secret-not-used-anywhere-real


# The dev server's origin, for the CORS allowlist.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173


# ============================================================================
# MODE A — stubbed HighLevel   ← ACTIVE, and the right default to commit
# ============================================================================
# The stand-in is served by the `api` function itself and mounted only under the
# emulator, so the whole OAuth loop runs offline: no network, no sandbox, no
# expiring authorization codes, nothing personal baked into the repo.
#
# Every automated test runs this way regardless of what is set here — the test
# scripts pass HL_TEST_* overrides, because CLAUDE.md requires HighLevel stubbed
# in CI and the suite must not depend on a sandbox that expires in six months.

HL_AUTHORIZE_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:5001/demo-genesis/asia-south1/api/__fake-hl
HL_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:5001/demo-genesis/asia-south1/api/__fake-hl
HL_CLIENT_ID=emulator-client-id
HL_CLIENT_SECRET=emulator-client-secret
HL_VERSION_ID=emulator-version-id
HL_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/api/oauth/callback


# ============================================================================
# MODE B — the real HighLevel, through an HTTPS tunnel
# ============================================================================
# For checking the integration against live HighLevel before deploying.
# Comment out MODE A above, uncomment the four lines at the end of this block,
# and replace <your-tunnel> throughout.
#
# **Local and temporary. Do not commit it** — `envLocal.spec.ts` will fail if
# you do, which is the point: a tunnel hostname is personal and stops resolving,
# so committed it silently breaks every other clone.
#
# HL_CLIENT_ID, HL_CLIENT_SECRET and HL_VERSION_ID stay commented out even in
# this mode. They fall through to functions/.env, so the real credentials are
# never written here.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Tunnel the Vite dev server:   ngrok http 5173
#   2. Register the callback on the marketplace app, Advanced Settings -> Auth:
#          https://<your-tunnel>/api/oauth/callback
#      byte for byte — HighLevel matches it exactly. If the app allows only one
#      redirect URL this replaces the deployed one; put it back before shipping.
#   3. Open the app at the tunnel URL, not at localhost — the callback answers a
#      *relative* redirect, so it resolves against the browser's origin.
#
# Authorization codes are single-use and short-lived: a failed attempt needs a
# fresh trip through consent, not a refresh.
#
# HL_AUTHORIZE_BASE=https://marketplace.gohighlevel.com
# HL_API_BASE=https://services.leadconnectorhq.com
# HL_REDIRECT_URI=https://<your-tunnel>/api/oauth/callback
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://<your-tunnel>
